.TH AVR\-TOKEN\-VIEW 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-token-view \- Show a token's details and grants, including a revoked or expired one.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr token view
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a token's details and grants, including a revoked or expired one.
.PP
The credential itself is never shown again after `avr token create`.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr token view <token-id>
    avr token view <token-id> --json grants
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    allow_vm_create, created_at, expires_at, grants, id, last_used_at,
    name, organization_id, revoked_at, revoked_reason, user_id,
    vm_create_count, vm_create_limit
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-token (1),
.BR avr-token-create (1),
.BR avr-token-list (1),
.BR avr-token-revoke (1)
